      "message": "It is requested from your comments in\nhttps://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/220518 (on Jan 15 in Patchset 2):\n\n\u003e This memory heap is not necessarily used right now. We need to update https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/BufferVk.cpp;drc\u003dff2449f5f5baaf56a34babaec640e9519a530623;l\u003d237 and https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/ResourceMemoryAllocatorVk.cpp;drc\u003d21fb99445f32855d3f3f213f2bcd1fa1baca1f59;l\u003d273 as well because buffers are no longer just \"HostLinear\", \"LinearReadMappable\", \"LinearWriteMappable\" but also \"HostMappable\" and \"LinearMappable\". So we could use a general refactor of that enum, to maybe be a bitset (MapRead|MapWrite|Host|LazilyAllocated|Opaque/Linear).\n\nI do this refactor for the implementation of `BufferMapExtendedUsage` on Vulkan. In the next patch I need to add a new memory kind `Device` and use (MapRead|MapWrite|Device) for (Storage | MapRead | MapWrite).",
